## UC17: Receive Low Stock Alert
**Scenario:** The system automatically alerts staff when stock falls below a threshold.
**Triggering event:** A sale reduces a product's stock below its reorder level.
**Actors:** System (initiator), Administrator / Inventory Staff (recipient)
**Related use cases:** View Inventory Report, Process Sale
**Stakeholders:** Administrator, Owner
**Preconditions:** Reorder level is configured for the product.
**Postconditions:** Staff are notified of the low-stock condition.

**Main flow:**
| Actor | System |
|---|---|
| — (system-initiated, following a sale) | 1.1 Check stock level after each sale |
| | 1.2 Compare against reorder level |
| | 1.3 Generate and send alert if below threshold |

**Exception conditions:** Reorder level not configured for the product — no alert can be generated.

**SSD:**
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant System as :System
    actor Administrator
    Note over System: triggered after each completed sale
    System->>System: checkStockLevel(productID)
    System-->>Administrator: lowStockAlert(productID, currentStock)
```

